.DS_Store

# NOTE: `.claude/` was ignored here until 2026-09-11, and that was the single
# biggest reason the three-gate enforcement did not work.
#
# The speckit-* skills are the layer that reads .specify/extensions.yml and runs
# the gate check. Ignoring .claude/ meant those skills were absent from the pushed
# repo entirely — a fresh clone got the gates, the constitution and check-gates.sh,
# but nothing that would ever invoke them. Enforcement has to travel with the repo
# or it is not enforcement, only a local habit.
#
# Tracking .claude/ is also what makes the skills discoverable to a Claude Code
# session, which is what allowed /speckit-plan and /check-gates to be invoked and
# tested for real.

# Condens content snapshots. The MECHANISM travels with this template; the CONTENT
# never does. These directories hold whole research reports — participant quotes,
# named customers, unredacted open-text feedback. Data gathered for a research
# purpose stays in that purpose (CLAUDE.md §10b, purpose limitation), and a template
# repo that gets forked and published is the wrong home for it.
#
# check-condens.sh degrades to a date-only comparison when they are absent and says
# so in its output, so a fresh clone is honest rather than quietly weaker.
condens-cache/*
!condens-cache/.gitkeep
condens-reconciled/*
!condens-reconciled/.gitkeep
